---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import TechnicalSpecimens from '../../components/dev/TechnicalSpecimens.mdx';
import '../../styles/home.css';
import '../../styles/projects.css';
import '../../styles/dev-tools.css';

const tokens = [
	['Page background', '--global-bg-color'],
	['Card background', '--global-card-bg-color'],
	['Section background', '--global-section-bg'],
	['Warm background', '--global-warm-bg'],
	['Warm border', '--global-warm-border'],
	['Text', '--global-text-color'],
	['Muted text', '--global-text-color-light'],
	['Divider', '--global-divider-color'],
	['Primary theme', '--global-theme-color'],
	['Hover', '--global-hover-color'],
	['Navbar', '--global-navbar-color'],
	['Navbar text', '--global-navbar-text-color'],
	['Navbar active', '--global-navbar-active-text-color'],
	['Navbar hover', '--global-navbar-hover-color'],
	['Blue accent', '--global-blue-accent'],
	['Homepage orange', '--homepage-orange-accent'],
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="Visual QA kitchen sink | Silvio Fanzon" description="Development-only inventory of current production patterns" />
		<meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow" />
	</head>
	<body class="standard-page" data-pagefind-ignore="all">
		<Header />
		<main class="content dev-content">
			<header class="compact-page-hero dev-hero">
				<p class="eyebrow">Development QA</p>
				<h1>Production pattern kitchen sink</h1>
				<p>Current site tokens, typography and reusable Astro-owned patterns rendered through their canonical production styles.</p>
				<nav class="dev-local-nav" aria-label="Development tools">
					<a href="/dev/kitchen-sink/" aria-current="page">Astro kitchen sink</a>
					<a href="/dev/quarto-kitchen-sink.html">Quarto kitchen sink</a>
					<a href="/dev/viewports/">Viewport dashboard</a>
				</nav>
			</header>

			<section class="dev-section" aria-labelledby="qa-palette">
				<header class="dev-section-header">
					<h2 id="qa-palette">Palette and tokens</h2>
					<p>These swatches reference the live production variables and change with the real theme control.</p>
				</header>
				<div class="dev-token-grid">
					{tokens.map(([role, token]) => (
						<article class="dev-token">
							<div class="dev-token-swatch" style={`--dev-swatch: var(${token})`}></div>
							<strong>{role}</strong>
							<code>{token}</code>
						</article>
					))}
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="dev-section" aria-labelledby="qa-technical">
				<header class="dev-section-header">
					<h2 id="qa-technical">Technical content</h2>
					<p>Genuine Astro MDX rendered through the configured Markdown, Shiki and KaTeX pipeline.</p>
				</header>
				<TechnicalSpecimens />
			</section>

			<section class="dev-section" aria-labelledby="qa-type">
				<header class="dev-section-header">
					<h2 id="qa-type">Typography and content</h2>
					<p>Current editorial hierarchy and ordinary readable content.</p>
				</header>
				<div class="dev-type-grid">
					<div class="dev-type-sample">
						<p class="eyebrow">Eyebrow / kicker</p>
						<h1>Heading level one</h1>
						<h2>Heading level two</h2>
						<h3>Heading level three</h3>
						<h4>Heading level four</h4>
						<p class="dev-prose">This longer paragraph checks the sustained reading measure, body rhythm and inline treatments. It contains an <a href="#qa-elements">inline link</a>, <strong>strong emphasis</strong>, <em>editorial emphasis</em> and <code>inline code</code> without introducing another typography system.</p>
						<p class="dev-muted">Muted secondary text using the current production text token.</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<p class="dev-sample-label">Lists</p>
						<ul>
							<li>Problem formulation</li>
							<li>Model implementation</li>
							<li>Evidence and communication</li>
						</ul>
						<ol>
							<li>Inspect</li>
							<li>Validate</li>
							<li>Explain</li>
						</ol>
						<hr />
						<pre class="dev-code"><code>result = model.fit(data)
validate(result)</code></pre>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="dev-section" aria-labelledby="qa-editorial">
				<header class="dev-section-header">
					<h2 id="qa-editorial">Editorial and interactive patterns</h2>
					<p>Representative canonical class-based patterns from current Astro pages.</p>
				</header>

				<div class="dev-sample">
					<p class="dev-sample-label">Section heading</p>
					<p class="dev-sample-description">Section introduction pairing an eyebrow, title, supporting text and optional destination link.</p>
					<div class="section-heading">
						<div>
							<p class="eyebrow">Section heading</p>
							<h2>Selected evidence</h2>
							<p class="section-intro">A production section header with its supporting introduction and action.</p>
						</div>
						<a class="section-link" href="/projects/">View projects →</a>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="dev-sample dev-project-example">
					<p class="dev-sample-label">Project card</p>
					<p class="dev-sample-description">Primary visual summary for project catalogue and featured work.</p>
					<article class="home-project-card">
						<div class="home-project-visual">
							<img src="https://www.silviofanzon.com/assets/img/projects/f1-benchmarking.svg" alt="Abstract Formula 1 benchmarking visual" />
						</div>
						<div class="home-project-copy">
							<p class="project-labels">Statistical modelling · Sports analytics · R</p>
							<h3>Who’s actually the best F1 driver?</h3>
							<p>A representative production card using the current project hierarchy.</p>
							<div class="home-project-actions">
								<a href="/projects/f1-time-rank-duality/">Read project <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
								<a href="https://github.com/sfanzon/F1-Paper-Code">Code</a>
							</div>
						</div>
					</article>
				</div>

				<div class="dev-sample">
					<p class="dev-sample-label">Capability rows</p>
					<p class="dev-sample-description">Compact text-led cards for communicating transferable skills or grouped evidence.</p>
					<div class="capability-grid">
						<article>
							<h3>Problem formulation</h3>
							<p>Turn an ambiguous question into explicit assumptions and measurable outcomes.</p>
						</article>
						<article>
							<h3>Implementation</h3>
							<p>Build reproducible numerical and statistical workflows.</p>
						</article>
						<article>
							<h3>Communication</h3>
							<p>Explain the evidence clearly for different audiences.</p>
						</article>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="dev-sample">
					<p class="dev-sample-label">Note row</p>
					<p class="dev-sample-description">Editorial list pattern combining date, topic metadata, summary and article action.</p>
					<div class="home-notes-list">
						<article class="home-note-row">
							<a class="home-note-row-visual" href="https://www.silviofanzon.com/notes/how-i-use-ai.html">
								<img src="https://www.silviofanzon.com/assets/img/notes/ai-agent-stack.svg" alt="AI-assisted technical workflow diagram" />
							</a>
							<div class="home-note-row-copy">
								<div class="home-note-row-meta">
									<time>30 July 2026</time>
									<span>AI · Workflow · Research</span>
								</div>
								<h3><a href="https://www.silviofanzon.com/notes/how-i-use-ai.html">How I use AI in technical work</a></h3>
								<p>A representative current note row with metadata, summary and action.</p>
								<a class="home-note-row-link" href="https://www.silviofanzon.com/notes/how-i-use-ai.html">Read note <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
							</div>
						</article>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="dev-sample">
					<p class="dev-sample-label">Publication row</p>
					<p class="dev-sample-description">Research citation pattern with thematic labels, bibliographic metadata and optional expandable detail.</p>
					<div class="home-publications-list">
						<article class="home-publication-row">
							<div class="publication-theme-rail">
								<span>Optimisation</span>
								<span>Numerical algorithms</span>
							</div>
							<div class="home-publication-main">
								<h3>Asymptotic linear convergence of Fully–Corrective Generalized Conditional Gradient methods</h3>
								<div class="paper-meta">
									<span>Kristian Bredies, Marcello Carioni, <u>Silvio Fanzon</u> and Daniel Walter</span>
									<span><em>Mathematical Programming</em> · 2024</span>
								</div>
								<div class="paper-actions">
									<a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s10107-023-01975-z">Journal</a>
									<details>
										<summary>Abstract</summary>
										<p>A representative expandable abstract using the production publication-row structure.</p>
									</details>
								</div>
							</div>
						</article>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="dev-sample">
					<p class="dev-sample-label">News disclosure</p>
					<p class="dev-sample-description">Compact chronological update with category metadata and optional supporting detail.</p>
					<div class="news-list">
						<details class="news-item">
							<summary>
								<time>Mar 2026</time>
								<span>PREPRINT</span>
								<strong>Formula 1 benchmarking preprint released</strong>
								<i aria-hidden="true"></i>
							</summary>
							<div>
								<p>A representative current News disclosure row.</p>
							</div>
						</details>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="dev-sample">
					<p class="dev-sample-label">Search-like input</p>
					<p class="dev-sample-description">Representative form control using the site's current input and action treatment.</p>
					<form class="dev-form-example" id="qa-elements">
						<label>
							Search-like input
							<input class="site-search-input" type="search" placeholder="Search site-wide" />
						</label>
						<button type="button">Action</button>
					</form>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="dev-section" aria-labelledby="qa-quarto">
				<header class="dev-section-header">
					<h2 id="qa-quarto">Quarto article QA</h2>
					<p>Scientific document patterns remain Quarto-owned and are inspected at their real merged routes.</p>
				</header>
				<nav class="dev-route-list" aria-label="Quarto article QA routes">
					<a href="/projects/f1-time-rank-duality/">F1 overview</a>
					<a href="/projects/f1-time-rank-duality/technical.html">F1 technical walkthrough</a>
					<a href="/projects/f1-time-rank-duality/code.html">F1 code and data</a>
				</nav>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
